  "number": 880,
  "state": "open",
  "locked": false,
  "title": "E64: Add a seed-driven any-language expansion protocol",
  "user": { "login": "konard", "id": 1431904, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard", "html_url": "https://github.com/konard", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false },
  "body": "Closes #706\n\n## Problem\n\nLanguage coordination was split between `agent-info.lino`, the hard-coded four-entry `IMPORT_LANGUAGES`, and handwritten round-trip cases. A fifth language therefore required Rust and CI edits, and partial coverage had no explicit contract preventing silent English substitution.\n\n## Solution\n\n- add `data/seed/languages.lino` as the registry for full and partial language status, suite coverage, detection claims, and explicit-gap behavior\n- derive bulk-import full-language requirements, CI coverage/parity guards, and the real translation round-trip matrix from that registry\n- add an audited Spanish partial slice: six meaning labels, greeting/identity/gap responses, operation vocabulary, and all 25 directed pair plus five same-language round trips\n- generate deterministic matrix and coverage evidence with `scripts/language-protocol.mjs`; Spanish passes 6/6 declared suites (100%) while general meaning coverage remains explicitly partial\n- add an Arabic sixth-language dry run that changes data only, passes 5/6 suites (83.3%), and reports the math-wrapper gap\n- preserve a real Formal AI + Agent CLI authorship session for one of five review leaves, with canonical artifact and raw client/server evidence\n- move the unknown-intent opener pools into `data/seed/unknown-openers.lino` and make the browser worker's\n  no-WASM fallbacks (script/marker detection, opener selection, known-response-language check) read the\n  hydrated registry, so registering a language stays data-only in the JS mirror too; the mirror grows a net\n  41 lines, re-baselining the worker line ratchet from 26,911 to 26,952 with the reason recorded next to the\n  #699/#701 precedents\n- give the Windows ARM64 desktop matrix a measured 40-minute budget after two otherwise-valid packages were cancelled at the former 30-minute cap, with a regression test that keeps the job bounded\n\n## Reproduction and verification\n\nBefore the fix, the issue-706 acceptance test failed all five cases because the registry, generated matrix/report, Spanish surfaces, Arabic candidate, and registry-driven CI contract did not exist. The legacy operation-vocabulary invariant also rejected any locale beyond the exact four-language set.\n\nAfter the fix:\n\n- `cargo test --test unit` — 2,286 passed, 3 ignored (on the merged `main`)\n- remaining `cargo test --tests` integration binaries — passed\n- `cargo test --test unit issue_706_any_language -- --nocapture` — 5 passed\n- bulk importer tests — 16 passed\n- translation round-trip specification — 7 passed, including registry-derived Spanish pairs\n- `cargo test --doc`\n- `cargo clippy --lib --bins --tests --all-features`\n- `cargo check --examples --all-features`\n- release build\n- language protocol generation check, language coverage/parity guards, seed mirror check, total/semantic closure, self-AST census, file-size and hardcoded-language checks\n- `node experiments/issue_706_worker_language_fallback.mjs` — the worker's no-WASM fallbacks resolve\n  en/ru/hi/zh/es against the real seed files, and an unlisted language borrows the `en` opener pool\n- desktop CI audit — 5 passed, including the measured Windows ARM64 budget regression\n- real self-host replay: session `ses_04be5591bffeIoDvic67voo3lE`; the metric validates 5.03% of changed authored lines (one of five review leaves)\n\nNo UI behavior changed, so screenshots are not applicable.\n\n",
